{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setLocalStoreDirectory"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"path","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"text":"discardingExistingCache","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event store’s directory, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" when no store is available.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"path"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", any cache already present for this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory must be deleted rather than loaded, and the backend must behave as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though it had never cached anything. The ensemble passes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" whenever the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store is being rebuilt, so a device starting over is guaranteed a full fetch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than a delta against a cursor from a previous incarnation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"discardingExistingCache"}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CustomCloudBackends"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backends that cache remote state between launches should store that cache inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this directory. Doing so ties the cache’s lifetime to the event store’s: when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store is removed or rebuilt, the stale cache goes with it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caching remote state anywhere with an independent lifetime (the system caches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory, for instance) is unsafe. Such a cache can outlive the event store it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"describes — surviving even app deletion — and a backend that then resumes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"incremental fetch against a rebuilt cloud may never be told about files that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"predate its stale cursor. The device sees a partial cloud and reports no error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Called before priming, whenever the ensemble knows its event store. It is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called for ensemble-independent operations such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/retrieveEnsembleIdentifiers(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", so implementations must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tolerate priming without it and simply forgo persistent caching in that case."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystemSetup"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Tells the file system which local directory belongs to the event store it is serving.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/cloudfilesystemsetup\/setlocalstoredirectory(_:discardingexistingcache:)"],"tra